```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{tocbasic}

\begin{document}

\tableofcontents

\section{Introduction}

This is the introduction section.

\section{Section 1}

This is section 1.

\section{Section 2}

This is section 2.

\section{Section 3}

This is section 3.

\end{document}
```
In this example, we start by loading the `tocbasic` package. Then, we use the `\tableofcontents` command to generate the table of contents automatically.

Note that the table of contents will appear at the beginning of the document, immediately after the section headings. If you want to control the placement of the table of contents, you can use the optional argument to the `\tableofcontents` command. For example, to place the table of contents at the end of the document, you can use:
```latex
\tableofcontents*
```
This will generate the table of contents at the end of the document, just before the list of references (if any).

