gpt-3.5-turbo:
Solution:

We can solve this problem by using logarithms. If n is a power of three, then we can find the value of x using logarithms. Specifically, x = log3(n).

We can use the Math.log() method in Java to compute the logarithm of n to the base 3. However, this method returns a double value, so we need to round it to the nearest integer and check if it equals x.

If n is negative or zero, then it cannot be a power of three. Therefore, we can return false for these cases.

Here is the Java code that implements this approach:

public class Solution {
    public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
        if (n <= 0) {
            return false;
        }
        int x = (int) Math.round(Math.log(n) / Math.log(3));
        return n == Math.pow(3, x);
    }
}

Time Complexity: O(1)

Space Complexity: O(1)

