To draw a chessboard using FEN notation in LaTeX, you can use the "skak" package. Below is a sample LaTeX code that includes all the required commands and packages to draw a chessboard based on FEN notation.

```
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{xskak}

\begin{document}

\newcommand{\fenboard}[1]{%
    \setchessboard{%
        showmover=false,
        moverstyle=triangle,
        movershift=-1.5ex,
        moverlift=-1.5ex
    }%
    \chessboard[setfen=#1]
}

\section{Chessboard with FEN Notation}

\subsection*{Example 1}
FEN: rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1

\fenboard{rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1}

\subsection*{Example 2}
FEN: 8/8/8/2k5/4K3/8/8/8 w - - 5 39

\fenboard{8/8/8/2k5/4K3/8/8/8 w - - 5 39}

\end{document}
```

